                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How long does a real digital transformation take?</h3>
                                        <p>3-5 years for a proper enterprise transformation. Anyone promising 12-18 months is either scoping small or overselling.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest cause of transformation failure?</h3>
                                        <p>Big-bang implementation without change management. Sequence, don't try to do everything at once.</p>
                                        <h3>How much should we budget for change management?</h3>
                                        <p>10-15% of total program budget. Skip this and adoption fails, ROI never materialises.</p>
                                        <h3>Should we hire a Big 4 consultancy or a boutique?</h3>
                                        <p>Big 4 for large multi-country programs. Boutique specialists for specific domains (ERP, data, digital customer experience). Blended is common.</p>
